design.systems 06 · TOKENS
// the bridge
Design tokens: the contract between design and code.
A token is a name for a decision. Once named, it can be referenced by Figma, by CSS, by Swift, by Kotlin, every surface speaks the same language.
tokens.json
What tokens get you
{
ONE CHANGE, EVERYWHERE
"color": {
"action": { "value": "#4A90F8" },
Update the action token; every button, link, and focus ring follows. No
find-and-replace across 40 components.
"surface": { "value": "#12161B" },
THEMING FOR FREE
"text": { "value": "#E8ECF1" }
},
Light/dark, brand variants, white-label all become token swaps, not parallel
codebases.
"space": [0, 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48],
"radius": { "sm": 4, "md": 8, "lg": 12 },
PLATFORM AGNOSTIC
"motion": {
"duration": { "fast": 150, "normal": 250 },
Tools like Style Dictionary export the same JSON to CSS, iOS, Android, Flutter.
One source, many targets.
"easing": { "standard": "cubic-bezier(.2,0,0,1)" }
}
}
